  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Establishment of a Multi-Agency Integrated Border Management Model in Sri Lanka - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phase II of the project will establish an Integrated InfoBorder System (IIBS), a foundation necessary for an integrated approach to border control in Sri Lanka. The project aims to strengthen the overarching migration management capacity of Sri Lanka, facilitating a more coordinated, intelligence-driven approach to border management through implementation of IIBS, and by strengthening the capacity of border agencies to implement associated policy /operational changes.&#xa0;Additional outcome under Phase II of the project will strengthen the capacity of national authorities to control spread of COVID-19 by enhancing health screening at pre-arrival as well as at the point of entry.</narrative>
  </description>
